  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/... \nIssued at 246 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nShower and thunderstorm potential returns area-wide again \nTuesday into Wednesday. Given this will be another northwest \nflow regime, it's tough to get too involved in the details. That\nsaid, the Tuesday storms do seem to have a rather healthy \nenvironment with increasing instability and modest deep layer \nshear supportive of more organized convection. SPC does have a \nday 4 15% risk for most of Iowa and WPC has put out a slight \nrisk for excessive rainfall for Tuesday. The pattern remains \nrelatively active through mid- week and then ridging begins to \nbuild through the second half of this week.",
